{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Living the Dream"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "I Got Accepted!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le16ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Passive Voice with Modals"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the receiver of the action, rather than the \u2018doer' of the action. <br/> You can also use <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs</span> in the passive voice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, something must/can/should be done by someone. It that case, we use some <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs</span>. Remember, after a modal verb, \"to\" is no necessary before the main verb. <br> For example: <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">This lesson must be practiced.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Modal verbs</span> can add meaning connected with <span class=\"underline\">suggestion </span> or <span class=\"underline\">obligation</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is the structure of a passive sentence:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + modal verb + be + past participle of the main verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">The company <span class=\"strong\">must be sold </span> on your performance.</span>  <br/><span class=\"italic\">Now that you have a new job, you car <span class=\"strong\">has to be fixed</span>.</span>  <br/><span class=\"italic\">The bills <span class=\"strong\">have to be paid</span> by tomorrow.</span> "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have/has/ must\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your car<br/> The bills\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has <br/> have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be <br/> to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fixed. <br/> paid by Tuesday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The employer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sold.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I also have some bills that must be paid and a student loan that should be addressed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The project should be presented next Friday."}, {"type": "example", "content": " It should be mentioned that I received another text from Boris today."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " What-Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> What-clauses </span> are used to help us focus on a particular part of the sentence and to emphasize what we want to say by introducing it as a relative clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span>  which are usually linked to the clause that we want to focus on with <span class=\"strong\">is </span> or <span class=\"strong\">was</span> ."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span>  I now need <span class=\"strong\">is </span> a new car</span> .<br/> <span class=\"italic\">A new car is <span class=\"strong\">what I </span> now need.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> I enjoyed most <span class=\"strong\">was </span> seeing their new office.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Seeing their new office <span class=\"strong\">was what </span> I enjoyed most.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses </span> are often used with verbs like <span class=\"strong\">adore</span>, <span class=\"strong\">dislike</span>, <span class=\"strong\">enjoy</span>, <span class=\"strong\">hate</span>, <span class=\"strong\">like</span>, <span class=\"strong\">loathe</span>, <span class=\"strong\">love</span>, <span class=\"strong\">need</span>, <span class=\"strong\">prefer</span>, <span class=\"strong\">want</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> I <span class=\"strong\">hate </span> most about going to a job interview is the waiting.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> I <span class=\"strong\">liked </span> most about their company was the people.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "What-clauses are also often used with <span class=\"strong\">does</span> /<span class=\"strong\">do</span> /<span class=\"strong\">did</span> and when we want to give emphasis to the whole sentence, rather than a particular clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The manager interviewed all the salespeople first.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> the manager <span class=\"strong\">did </span> first <span class=\"strong\">was </span> interview all the salespeople. </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "These sentences are useful in writing where we cannot use intonation for emphasis, but they are also often used in speech."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What I want you to do is to make some goals for this job. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "What I want is a used car.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "What he wanted was to tell me about another editorial assistant job. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "What worries me is that you are new and if Adam doesn't do a good job, it may reflect badly on you."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pumped up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "motivated; excited"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That job seminar has me so pumped up right now!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you need to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "right out of the gate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "from the beginning "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think it turned the interviewer off right out of the gate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to start off on the wrong foot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to begin in an awkward or unpleasant way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  This interview has started off on the wrong foot. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ideal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "perfect"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your skills and experience will be an ideal fit for our team."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sounds like a plan"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that's a good idea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Let's meet Thursday? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Bianca</span>: Sounds like a plan."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "In groups of three, brainstorm ideas for a dream job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you have just gotten your dream."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write your future goals for your dream job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "One partner writes the goals for now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "One writes the goals for the near future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "One writes the goals for the distant future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your stories as a group and compare your results."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I imagine attaining my dream job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write future goals using Future Tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my stories with my group clearly."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about goals and experiences related to jobs. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss future plans."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about facts and courses of actions."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What is the next job you would like to do?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What goals would you have for that job?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's 